PART E -- Tournament Analysis on abstract proof quotients
  Pairwise observable=(obligation_failures, min_margin, generated_fidelity, auditability).
  Switch/gauge: lower failures win; ties use larger margin, then fidelity.
    miss_zeta_generated_word: score=6, metric=(0, Fraction(20, 16807), 7, 8), note=best quotient: generated residual pressure before scalarization
    coherent_context_merge: score=5, metric=(0, Fraction(20, 16807), 6, 7), note=tests generated OR/deletion contexts, not only singletons
    slope_band_signed_sum: score=4, metric=(0, Fraction(20, 16807), 5, 7), note=preserves Angle A seven-band debt/rescue information
    unbanded_death_chain_kernel: score=3, metric=(0, Fraction(20, 16807), 4, 6), note=actual singleton context scalar; all frontier rows pass
    hitcount_FOSD: score=2, metric=(72, Fraction(-33, 12005), 2, 4), note=would prove all increasing kernels, but fails on many rows
    raw_sparse_coordinates: score=1, metric=(72, Fraction(-1, 1), 0, 3), note=keeps residual packets but scalarizes before context; known false quotient
    per_band_monotonicity: score=0, metric=(192, Fraction(-33, 12005), 3, 5), note=too strong; useful only as a signed-debt ledger
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  SCCs=[['miss_zeta_generated_word'], ['coherent_context_merge'], ['slope_band_signed_sum'], ['unbanded_death_chain_kernel'], ['hitcount_FOSD'], ['raw_sparse_coordinates'], ['per_band_monotonicity']]
  Hamiltonian_path_count=1
  Tie Hamiltonian path is the score order above.

SYNTHESIS
  The singleton death-chain margin is positive on every S64 sparse-coordinate
  frontier row and on the extra bounded singleton slices tested here.
  However, first-order hit-count dominance and per-band monotonicity both fail.
  The live proof object should therefore be a signed seven-band death-chain
  ledger plus the generated miss-zeta/context-merge monotonicity lemma.
